   "title": "Note",
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Sprite normal maps\nModel-free and pixel-exact: a rounded 'pillow' from each sprite's silhouette (`inflate`, `radius`) plus relief from its shading (`detail`). Feed a whole spritesheet — every frame gets its normals in the same layout, ready as the engine's normal texture.\n**Engines:** Godot 4 → CanvasTexture `normal_texture` (OpenGL). Unity URP 2D → Sprite *Secondary Textures* `_NormalMap` (OpenGL). Unreal Paper2D → DirectX convention.\nPixel art: `detail_blur` 0. HD art: 1–2, or use 28b."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
